      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

Alibaba is rolling out what it calls China’s most powerful AI chip, an accelerator to compete with Nvidia and underpin a massive expansion of data center capacity in coming years.

Global AI stocks rallied, with Taiwanese shares returning to a record high. This after Meta's new artificial intelligence agent, Muse, quickly rose to the top of mobile app charts, a sign that the social media company is gaining traction in the increasingly crowded market for consumer AI assistants.

Today's guest: Lauren van Biljon, Allspring Global Investments, Senior Portfolio Manager, Global Fixed Income Team.
